{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTMaxCorner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTMaxCorner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramCorner","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.exists_corner_entry_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.exists_corner_entry_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTMaxCorner.lean#L43-L52","doc":"**A non-empty diagram has a max-value corner.** Some cell of `T` carries the top value `|μ|`, and\nthat cell is a removable corner — the cell the forward branching map deletes.  (Existence comes from\nsurjectivity of the entry bijection onto `{1, …, |μ|}`; cornerness from the lemma above.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_of_entry_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_of_entry_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTMaxCorner.lean#L22-L41","doc":"**The max-value cell is a removable corner.** If a cell `c` of a standard tableau `T` carries the\ntop value `|μ|`, then `c` is a removable corner of `μ`: both `(c.1+1, c.2)` and `(c.1, c.2+1)` lie\noutside `μ`, since either would carry a value `> |μ|` by the strict column/row law. ","signatureChunk":0}]}